> **"Before final verdict, one thing I tell every client: buy the [men's ring](/mens-diamond-engagement-ring) last, not first. Lock in the width by measuring your finger at the widest point — usually mid-afternoon when your hand is slightly warm. Measure three times across two different days. Only then choose a ring. I've seen men measure once at 9am on a cold morning, buy an 8mm band, and return it after the ceremony because it wouldn't come off after dancing. Width selection is not a preference. It is a measurement problem. Measure correctly, and every ring in this guide will serve you well."**
> — Farzana Hasan, diamond expert | [About Farzana](/about-farzana/)

